## The "5 already covered" framing didn't hold up

Checked before trusting it, per the trigger's own "confirm coverage" instruction: two cell names
(`m-ta-calibration-probe`, `m-ta-dwell`, `m-satta-dwell`, `m-sat-dwell`) each have more than one
real run directory, and the earlier `all-panels-20260813/` sweep's PNGs carry no run ID in their
title and no bundle saved alongside them -- no way to confirm which specific run each one actually
came from. More directly: `planning/ta-pokprod-rerun-results-20260813.md` itself says **"No viz
output exists for any run in this doc"**, which contradicts "5 of 7 already covered." Resolved by
re-extracting all 7 fresh rather than guessing -- output now at
`session-notes/review-samples/backlog-rerun-20260813/<cell-name>/{bundle.json,coverage.json,panels.png}`,
one subdirectory per run, unambiguous provenance.

## One run had 4 parallel leaves, not one

`dean-20260813-130251-004` (the parallelism-4 validation) has 4 separate results leaves under its
`results/` dir, not one -- extracted and rendered all 4 (`m-ta-calibration-probe-p4_1` through
`_4`) rather than picking one arbitrarily. None of the 4 has a captured `controller.log`.

